& [IdentityAudit] passes
  + exact source and manifest identity match
  + five I03A input artifacts match measured path bytes and SHA256
  + current formation makes no Cargo Rust target or policy mutation

& [HistoricalEvidence] remains authoritative within scope
  + preserved 18:53 denial binds exact helper events cargo initiator policy and pre-execution boundary
  + later event rollover neither weakens nor strengthens that preserved evidence
  + no present release pass exists

& [RetentionObservation] is point-in-time source evidence
  + circular mode size record count oldest and newest values describe one read-only query
  + raw query output was not separately sealed as a standalone event bundle
  + the measured source preserves the manager observation but cannot become a substitute for future raw XML capture
  + canonical protocol uses the observation to justify immediate capture rather than treating its counters as permanent constants

& [Delineation1] no retained Cantor event differs from no Cantor denial
  + the log oldest timestamp was later than the preserved denial
  + absence in the rolled log is unknown historical retention not proof of admission
  + future no-event support requires one bounded attempt with intact pre/post channel continuity

& [Delineation2] command result differs from policy result
  + native exit code terminal state stdout and stderr describe command execution
  + Code Integrity events describe host policy decisions
  + artifact inspection describes produced carriers
  + admitted_pass requires the applicable conjunction rather than any single source

& [Delineation3] file existence differs from launch
  + generated artifact may be blocked before execution
  + cached artifact may exist without participation in the attempt
  + final success cannot be inferred from intermediate file presence

& [Delineation4] Authenticode status differs from enterprise-policy admission
  + Get-AuthenticodeSignature-style observation reports signature and chain information under its API context
  + Code Integrity applies an active policy level to an attempted load
  + either may inform evidence but neither substitutes silently for the other

& [Correction1] channel continuity must detect clear reset or replacement
  + capture channel log mode maximum size record count oldest newest record ids and log metadata before and after
  + a post watermark lower than pre watermark or inconsistent channel identity makes event evidence incomplete
  + EventRecordID comparison is only valid inside one continuous channel generation

& [Correction2] environment capture is allowlisted
  + record only variables needed to reproduce Cargo Rust target feature offline and policy context
  + never dump complete process environment command history credentials tokens certificates private keys or user secrets
  + secret-bearing values are excluded and presence may be represented without content only when required

& [Correction3] future exact command identity cannot be fully formed before the authorized four-surface diff and lock exist
  + package test feature locked offline and debug or release intent are stable
  + exact Cargo executable digest arguments toolchain target directory expected test count and lock digest bind the future attempt
  + formation leaves these as required future fields rather than placeholders in an active record

& [Correction4] fresh target prevents cached execution claims but does not forbid locked source cache
  + source cache is read-only input with exact crate checksums and Cargo lock
  + target directory begins absent or empty and is unique
  + no copied hard-linked or warmed build output enters it

& [Correction5] capture failure is atomic for admission
  + evidence may preserve partial output
  + a missing raw event range truncated stream wrapper fault channel reset or exhausted budget prevents admitted_pass
  + retry is a new attempt with predecessor reference

& [Correction6] log volume can exceed configured capture limits
  + filters may project relevant event ids and paths but raw selected events must remain intact
  + if event attribution cannot be bounded without dropping potentially relevant records the attempt is evidence_incomplete
  + truncation never becomes silence

& [DualHemisphereGenerative] supports immediate watermark capture fresh targets one-command attempts raw plus normalized evidence and staged gate envelopes
& [DualHemisphereCritical] attacks rollover aggregation cache substitution localized message dependence environment-secret leakage channel reset and signature-policy collapse

& [SJSDecision] is protocol formation permitted
  + preserve the historical block
  + add continuous-channel identity allowlisted environment and atomic capture requirements
  + retain future exact command binding and non-circular review envelope
  + issue no execution or policy authority

& [AuditDisposition] is SJS_input_accepted_protocol_formation_only
